  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMP Support to Ukraine in Accounting for Missing Persons</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the Ukrainian authorities in accounting for large numbers of missing persons to judicial standards that will make it possible to hold perpetrators of atrocities to account, provide the public with credible information regarding disappeared persons and related crimes, and secure the rights of families of the missing. ICMP will support further development and strengthening of Ukraine&#x2019;s technical capacity for dedicated and sustainable impartial investigations into missing persons cases. It will support meaningful participation by Ukraine&#x2019;s civil society and family associations, especially those that are women-led, in the missing persons process, facilitate intergovernmental and in-country cooperation and raise awareness about the central role of this issue in security and peacebuilding. The project is gender mainstreamed.</narrative>
  </description>
